  "fanTake": "The Patriots ground out a 20-3 win at home against Pittsburgh on Sunday, and while the scoreboard is absolutely delightful, the underlying performance tells a more complicated story. Our offense managed just -0.07 EPA per play—worse than average—and converted only 33% of our third downs and 33% of our red-zone trips, both well below league norms; the good news is that our defense absolutely smothered the Steelers, allowing -0.36 EPA per play and holding them to just one field goal across 12 third-down attempts and a single red-zone trip. Rhamondre Stevenson was our most impactful player by win probability added, contributing 3%, which feels about right for a day where we won convincingly without sparkling offensively. It's the kind of victory that feels good in the standings but leaves you wanting more from the offense—we're still finding our rhythm, even if our defense is doing enough to mask the issues for now.",
